XSS: model commentary went into innerHTML unescaped (dashboard/index.html)

Auto-commit hook wrote the provisional subject; this note is the real message.
Covers 3224c70 (commentary) and 40cb53c (alert title).

THE HOLE. The journal renderer did:
    ${t.commentary.replace(/\n/g,"<br>")}
straight into an innerHTML template literal. t.commentary is MODEL OUTPUT, written
by Claude from market data and news it was fed. A <script> or <img onerror=...>
reaching a commentary string executed in the dashboard. This is exactly the
standing rule that API responses are data and never instructions - and it does not
need an attacker, only a quoted "<" in a headline.

THE FIX, and the order is the whole thing:
    ${escapeHtml(t.commentary).replace(/\n/g,"<br>")}
Escape FIRST, then substitute \n -> <br>. Reversed, our own <br> would be escaped
to literal "&lt;br&gt;" and the panel would show markup as text. Reuses the
existing escapeHtml at :3511 rather than adding a fourth escaper - the file
already had two hand-rolled duplicates at :4375 and :5494.

PROVEN with the real escapeHtml lifted out of the shipped file, not a
reimplementation. 4 payloads carried live markup before, all 4 inert after;
newline still renders as a real <br>; "P&L" -> "P&amp;L" (& escaped first, not
double-escaped).

MY FIRST TEST ORACLE WAS WRONG AND REPORTED A FALSE FAILURE. It regexed the
output for /on\w+=/, which still matches the literal text inside
"&lt;img src=x onerror=&quot;...&quot;&gt;" - a completely inert string. Matching
attack substrings in escaped text tests nothing. Replaced with the structural
invariant: strip our own <br>, then assert zero surviving '<' or '>', which is
exactly the condition under which innerHTML can create no element.

SECOND SITE (40cb53c), NOT an injection, fixed anyway: the alerts hover title did
String(a.message).replace(/"/g,'&quot;'). Inside a double-quoted attribute the only
way out is a literal ", which that did stop - but it left & unescaped, so "P&L" and
"&amp;" round-tripped mangled. Now escapeHtml, which handles & and " in the right
order.

NOT FIXED, deliberately: :5069 builds getElementById('${cid}') from
cid="jct-"+t.ticket. That is a numeric broker ticket, not model output.

LIVE NOW, no restart needed - express.static (:11154) reads from disk per request
and sets Cache-Control: no-cache on .html. Different from the setEncoding fix in
2a4fd3e, which waits for the next server start.

Verified: all inline scripts parse; firing set untouched (this is a render path).
